# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# MediTrack client environment (Vite).
#
# Vite exposes ONLY variables prefixed with VITE_ to the browser, and it INLINES
# them at BUILD time. That means anything here is public — it ships inside the
# JavaScript bundle — and changing it requires a rebuild/redeploy. Never put a
# secret (API key, database URL, JWT secret) in this file.
#
# Copy to `client/.env` for local development. On Vercel, set the same keys
# under Project → Settings → Environment Variables instead of committing a file.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

# Base URL the SPA uses for API calls.
#
# Recommended: leave this as the default relative path. The frontend and API
# then share an origin (Vercel rewrites /api/* to the Render service — see
# vercel.json), which keeps the session cookie first-party and avoids CORS.
#
# Only set an absolute URL if you deliberately call the API cross-origin
# (in that case also set COOKIE_SAME_SITE=none on the server):
#   VITE_API_BASE=https://your-service.onrender.com/api/v1
VITE_API_BASE=/api/v1

# Dev only: where the Vite dev server proxies /api requests. Read by
# vite.config.js in Node while running `npm run dev` (it is not inlined into the
# bundle). Defaults to http://localhost:5000.
# VITE_API_TARGET=http://localhost:5000
